    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0455" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v17p2/pg423"/>

                <head>163. Memorandum From Secretary of State Vance to President Carter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d163-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-03-27">March 27, 1979</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here are items unrelated to East Africa.]</p>
                <p>4. <hi rendition="#italic">Uganda:</hi> Nyerere has told us that over the weekend
                    Quadafi sent him an ultimatum giving Tanzania 24 hours to withdraw from Uganda.
                    Nyerere ignored this threat and is continuing to pursue his military campaign
                    against Amin, but he has expressed his concern to us and other Western
                    representatives and has asked us for our assessment of Libyan involvement in
                    Uganda. We will give him our intelligence on <pb facs="0456" n="424"
                        xml:id="pg424"/> Libya’s military capability.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d163-f2"
                    /> Our initial estimate is that the Libyan threat contains a large element of
                        bluff.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d163-f3"/></p>
                <p>Ugandan exile leaders meeting in Tanzania have elected an 11-member council as a
                    provisional government. The council, which is representative of the regional and
                    ethnic groups of Uganda, plans to establish itself in southern Uganda.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here are items unrelated to East Africa.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject
                    File, Box 21, Evening Reports (State) 3/79. Secret. Carter initialed the
                    memorandum and wrote “Cy” in the upper right corner.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f2" n="2" xml:id="d163-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 76729 to Dar es Salaam, the Department instructed the Ambassador to
                    pass along U.S. intelligence on Libyan involvement in Uganda; the United States
                    estimated that there were fewer than 500 Libyan troops there and that Libyan air
                    support was limited to a single plane. (National Archives, RG 59, Central
                    Foreign Policy File, P840128–1920)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f3" n="3" xml:id="d163-f3-content">
                <p>Carter wrote “I agree” in the left margin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
